        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prior violation on property and Priority"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763578987133"
          },
          "code": "PRIOR_VIOLATION_ON_PROPERTY_AND_PRIORITY",
          "id": "1763578823125",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763578823127_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with:\n\nIncidentList = {{$context.$variables.IncidentList}}\nCaseList = {{$context.$variables.CaseList}}\nThe incoming incidents fields, including IssueDescription (as {{$context.$variables.IssueDescription}}) and Priority {{$context.$variables.IncidentDetail.Priority}}.\n\n1. Prior Violation Retrieval\n- Determine Match Key: For each record, if ParcelIdEntered is present, use it as the match key.\n  If ParcelIdEntered is missing, use PropertyAddress1 as the match key.\n  Consider only records with the same match key as the incoming incident/case.\n- Filter Records From both IncidentList and CaseList:\n  Select only records where Status equals 'ORA_CLS' and ClosedDate is less than 3 months.\n\n2. Priority Recommendation\nAnalyze the incoming incident and the results of Prior Violations from step 1.\nRecommend whether the priority should be escalated to \"ORA_H\" (High), using the following criteria:\n\n-Prior Violations:\nIf there are any prior violations from above, recommend \"ORA_H\".\nState in the summary how many prior violations were found.\n- Sentiment Analysis:\nAnalyze the {{$context.$variables.IssueDescription}} of the incoming incident for urgency, severity, or negative sentiment (such as urgent language, safety concerns, public risk, threats, etc).\nIf the sentiment indicates high urgency, safety, or potential harm, recommend setting the Priority to \"ORA_H\".\nIf the Priority of the incoming Incident is already \"ORA_H\", then do not recommend setting the Priority to \"ORA_H\"\nBriefly explain the key phrases or detected sentiment that contributed to this recommendation.\n\nIMPORTANT : Do not use any special characters or quotes for Summary and Detail fields."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"PriorViolationsCheck\": {\n   \"ViolationsFound\": [true|false],\n    \"ViolationCount\": [integer-total number of matches],\n    \"Summary\": \"[ Write a single grammatically correct sentence describing the result. If a prior violation is found, state: 'A prior violation (IncidentId [ID]) was closed on [Date].' Do not mention match key or technical details. If no prior violation is found, state: 'No prior violations were found in the last three months.']'\",\n    \"Details\": \"[ Write a clear and complete sentence summarizing the result of the prior violation check. If prior violations are found, mention the details on the first match found -IncidentId(s) and include relevant close date(s) and, if available, address. If there were no prior violations, simply state that none were found.]\",\n    \"matches\": [\n      {\n        \"TransactionKey\": [integer],\n        \"TransactionId\": \"[string]\",\n        \"IssueType\": \"[string]\",\n        \"IssueSubtype\": \"[string]\",\n        \"SubmitDate\": \"[YYYY-MM-DD]\",\n        \"Status\": \"[string]\",\n        \"IntakeSource\":\"[string]\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"PriorityRecommendation\": {\n    \"UpdatePriority\": \"[true|false]\",\n    \"RecommendedPriority\": \"[ORA_H or ORA_N]\",\n    \"Summary\": \"[Summary of why priority should be escalated (e.g., X prior violations found, urgent language detected in description, etc.) mention 'High' if ORA_H or 'Normal' if ORA_N]\",\n    \"Details\": \"[Mention if the Priority needs to be escalated and a short sentence on why if it needs to be escalated mention 'High' if ORA_H or 'Normal' if ORA_N]\"\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Duplicate Checker"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763578987133"
          },
          "code": "DUPLICATE_CHECKER",
          "id": "1763578846058",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763578846060_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with an IncidentList= {{$context.$variables.IncidentList}} and a CaseList = {{$context.$variables.CaseList}} , each containing records describing incidents or cases at various property addresses.\nYour task is to determine whether an incoming incident is a duplicate based on matching criteria, and to recommend which item, if any, should be considered the parent/active record to close the incoming incident as its duplicate.\n\nYour objectives:\n\n1. Combine Arrays and Strict Filter\n\n- Create a new array called dataset by concatenating IncidentList and CaseList.\n- Read Status exactly as provided in the source record. \n- Exclude any record whose raw Status is:\n   ORA_CLS\n   ORA_CMP\n   ORA_VOD\n- Validation:\nAfter filtering, verify that dataset contains NO records with Status ORA_CLS, ORA_CMP, or ORA_VOD.\nIf any exist, remove them before continuing.\n\n2. Duplicate Check:\n- From the filtered dataset, identify records with the same IssueType == {{$context.$variables.IssueType}} AND same IssueSubtype == {{$context.$variables.IssueSubtype}} , as the incoming incident and store in array called matches.\n- If matches.length > 0, duplicate(s) found. If matches.length === 0, then no duplicate found.\n\n3. AI Decision Which to Close As Duplicate:\n- If duplicates are found, determine the match with the earliest reported/submitted/created date as CloseAsDuplicate.\n- This parent should appear as the first item in the matches array.\n- Suggest setting the parents priority to High (include in summary).\n\n4. Before returning the final answer, run one final validation:\nremove any record from matches whose raw Status is ORA_CLS, ORA_CMP, or ORA_VOD.\nIf that removes all matches, return no duplicate found.\n\nIMPORTANT : Do not use any special characters or quotes for Summary and Detail fields.\n\nFOr Output Purpose Only: Status with Field Mapping for output only: Map the status lookup to meaning in the output json\n\nORA_REP -> Reported\nORA_CLS -> Closed\nORA_INS -> Inspection\nORA_VIO -> Violation\nORA_UND -> Undetermined\nORA_LEGL -> Legal"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"DuplicateCheck\": {\n    \"DuplicateFound\": [true|false],\n    \"DuplicateCount\": [integer],\n    \"Summary\": \"[One sentence summary, e.g., '2 incidents/cases at the same parcel with matching subtype and similar description.']\",\n    \"Details\": \"[List each matching incident or case on its own line. For incidents, use: - [IncidentId] with status [Status with Field Mapping] was submitted on [SubmitDate]. For cases, use: - [CaseId] with status [Status with Field Mapping] was created on [CreationDate]. After each bullet point, insert a line break so each record appears on its own line.]\"\n    \"CloseAsDuplicate\": \"[IncidentId or CaseId of incident recommended for closure]\",\n    \"CloseAsDuplicateIntakeSource\": \"[IntakeSource of incident recommended for closure]\",\n    \"matches\": [\n      {\n        \"TransactionKey\": [integer],\n        \"TransactionId\": \"[string]\",\n        \"IssueType\": \"[string]\",\n        \"IssueSubtype\": \"[string]\",\n        \"SubmitDate\": \"[YYYY-MM-DD]\",\n        \"Status\": \"[string - with Status Field Mapping]\",\n        \"IntakeSource\":\"[string]\",\n       \"reason\": \"[Describe why this transaction is a duplicate, e.g., 'Matched on parcel and similar description.']\",\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Related Transactions on Property"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1763578987133"
          },
          "code": "RELATED_TRANSACTIONS_ON_PROPERTY",
          "id": "1763578872524",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763578872525_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Combine the results from {{$context.$variables.RelatedCases}}, {{$context.$variables.RelatedPermits}} and {{$context.$variables.RelatedIncidents}} with their respective counts and return the output.\n\nCombine the results from {{$context.$variables.RelatedCases}}, {{$context.$variables.RelatedPermits}}, and {{$context.$variables.RelatedIncidents}} excluding any incident with incidentId equal to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.IncidentId}} . Use the filtered incidents list and its count in the output.\n\nIMPORTANT : Do not use any special characters or quotes for Summary and Detail fields."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"RelatedTransactions\" : {\n  \"Details\": \"[Summarize only what is present in a user-friendly way. If nothing is found, say: 'No related transactions were found.' If one type is found, say: 'Found X related [item type] (ID(s): ...).' If multiple items of the same type are found, include all IDs. If multiple types are found, combine naturally without listing all categories explicitly. For each type, if the found count is greater than 0, include the IDs: 'Found X case(s)[ (IDs: ...)], Y permit(s)[ (IDs: ...)], and Z incident(s)[ (IDs: ...)].' ]\",\n    \"Summary\": \"[Craft a concise, grammatically correct summary of the findings. For example: 'No related transactions were found; or one incident was reported.' or 'Found 2 related cases, 1 permit, and 3 incidents.']\",\n    \"Case\": {\n      \"Count\" : Count {{$context.$variables.RelatedCases}},\n      \"Results\" : [Assign {{$context.$variables.RelatedCases}}]\n   },\n   \"Permits\": {\n      \"Count\" : Count {{$context.$variables.RelatedPermits}},\n      \"Results\" : [Assign {{$context.$variables.RelatedPermits}}]\n   },\n  \"Incidents\": {\n      \"Count\" : Count {{$context.$variables.RelatedIncidents}},\n      \"Results\" : [Assign {{$context.$variables.RelatedIncidents}}]\n   }\n }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Incident Checker Output"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764780043273"
          },
          "code": "INCIDENT_CHECKER_OUTPUT",
          "id": "1763578987133",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763578987134_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Combine output from the following nodes into a single JSON object and store the result in response:\n\n output of the Priority agent: {{$context.$nodes.PRIOR_VIOLATION_ON_PROPERTY_AND_PRIORITY.$output}}\n output of the Duplicate Checker : {{$context.$nodes.DUPLICATE_CHECKER.$output}}\n output of the Subtype Validation agent: {{$context.$nodes.ISSUE_SUBTYPE_VALIDATION_AGENT.$output}}\n output of the Related Transactions: {{$context.$nodes.RELATED_TRANSACTIONS_ON_PROPERTY.$output}}\nIn addition, determine and add a \"RecommendedAction\" array to this JSON by following these rules:\n\nIf DuplicateFound is true in the output of the Duplicate Checker, add \"ORA_DUPLICATE\" to the RecommendedAction array.\nIf UpdatePriority is true in the output of the Priority agent, add \"ORA_PRIORITY\" to the RecommendedAction array.\nIf RerouteNeeded is true in the output of the Subtype Validation agent, add \"ORA_REROUTE\" to the RecommendedAction array.\nIf all three flags above (DuplicateFound, UpdatePriority, RerouteNeeded) are false, then add both \"ORA_ASSIGN_TECHNICIAN\" and \"ORA_SCHEDULE_INSPECTION\" to the array.\nOnly include a code if its condition is satisfied.\n\nOutput the full combined JSON object, Ensure each object has Details and Summary."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"RelatedTransactions\": {},\n  \"PriorViolationsCheck\": {},\n  \"Reroute\": {},\n  \"RecommendedAction\": [],\n  \"DuplicateCheck\": {},\n  \"PriorityRecommendation\": {}\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
